<title>USA: Dow industrials fall 50 points.</title>
<headline>Dow industrials fall 50 points.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow Jones industrial average lost more than 50 points in early afternoon trading Thursday as blue-chip stocks tracked weakness in the bond market.</p>
<p>At 12:45 p.m. EDT, the index of 30 blue-chip issues was down 50.21 points at 7,639.77, which activated the New York Stock Exchange's limits on program trading. The 30-year Treasury fell 10/32, or $3.125 on a $1,000 bond, raising its yield to 6.76 percent from 6.74 percent on Wednesday.</p>
